Feels like you got kinda tougher.

256
00:09:08,670 --> 00:09:09,460
Really?!

257
00:09:10,790 --> 00:09:14,040
Come to think of it, my Sword Mastery skill
is all the way at level three.

258
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:19,420
Plus, the expansion of my inventory gave me
more space to buff my endurance and attack!

259
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:21,420
I guess so!

260
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:24,710
I wonder if that aroma skill
from earlier has any effect in battle.

261
00:09:24,830 --> 00:09:26,540
Like, maybe it can give boosts?

262
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:31,750
Actually, wait. I just remembered Fido was my
first summon with an attack skill called "Chomp."

263
00:09:32,170 --> 00:09:36,460
I really wanna try it out,
but I shouldn't use it on people...

264
00:09:37,290 --> 00:09:38,380
What's the matter?

265
00:09:39,790 --> 00:09:40,790
It's nothing.

266
00:09:48,710 --> 00:09:51,670
I swear I've thrown more than
20,000 of these at this point,

267
00:09:51,670 --> 00:09:53,710
but there's no sign of my skill leveling up...

268
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:58,580
Big Brudder! This is boring!

269
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:00,710
Sorry. Wait just a little longer, okay?

270
00:10:01,130 --> 00:10:05,080
I already have to look after Mash and help Mommy
with the chores since she's pregnant.

271
00:10:05,330 --> 00:10:08,580
Besides, I should really be focusing
on increasing my summon level instead.

272
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:11,250
This just isn't worth the time it takes.

273
00:10:11,790 --> 00:10:14,880
So I guess I'll quit practicing my "Throw" skill.

274
00:10:15,290 --> 00:10:19,210
Except I hate to think I'm just
one toss away from leveling up.

275
00:10:19,330 --> 00:10:21,130
That makes it impossible to quit!

276
00:10:21,130 --> 00:10:23,380
Hey! What're these trees?

277
00:10:27,710 --> 00:10:29,540
Shucks, I'm not sure.

278
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:32,580
We practically have a garden now.

279
00:10:32,790 --> 00:10:34,330
But they're really just taking up space...

280
00:10:35,330 --> 00:10:37,830
I figured out a few things out from testing.

281
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:43,790
Mainly that Appo's skill, Aroma, can shorten
MP recovery time from six hours to five hours.

282
00:10:44,250 --> 00:10:46,330
Which enables me to do even more daily activities.

283
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:50,500
But honestly, it feels like
I'll never have enough time...

284
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,540
Daddy sure is late.

285
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:07,790
Yeah. Even though he said
he would be working close by today...

286
00:11:08,420 --> 00:11:10,210
C'mon, Rodin! Hang in there!

287
00:11:12,210 --> 00:11:13,960
Careful not to drop him, fellas!

288
00:11:17,750 --> 00:11:19,830
Listen! We've almost got you home!

289
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:25,790
We made it! Your family's here, Rodin!

290
00:11:30,750 --> 00:11:32,040
He got hit bad...

291
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:33,960
Took a boar fang right to the gut.

292
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:44,000
THE HARDCORE GAMER DOMINATES

293
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:44,000
IN ANOTHER WORLD WITH GARBAGE BALANCING

294
00:11:46,710 --> 00:11:47,580
Oh, honey...

295
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:56,000
Man, looks like they straight up
cauterized the wound.

296
00:11:56,630 --> 00:12:00,710
We managed to keep him alive.
Thanks to a healing herb.

297
00:12:01,040 --> 00:12:01,920
Healing herb?

298
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:03,960
A Muellerze Flower.

299
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:05,380
Wait, really?

300
00:12:05,710 --> 00:12:08,540
But how did you even get something so valuable?

301
00:12:08,710 --> 00:12:10,630
Remember when the knights came the other day?

302
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:13,170
As part of their apology
for what happened with Krena,

303
00:12:13,460 --> 00:12:15,750
the knight captain gave me some gold coins.

304
00:12:16,750 --> 00:12:19,210
We would've been screwed without those.

305
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:22,210
Well, that stupid commoner
is to blame for all this!

306
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:26,080
Enough is enough!
Let's put our collective foot down!

307
00:12:26,290 --> 00:12:27,210
C'mon, Gerda!

308
00:12:29,670 --> 00:12:31,210
What's going on?

309
00:12:36,460 --> 00:12:38,460
Aw, don't fret, Mash.

310
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:40,420
It's all gonna be okay.

311
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:43,170
Let's give them some peace.
You fellas should head home.

312
00:12:43,630 --> 00:12:45,710
Don't do anything rash, hear me?

313
00:12:50,330 --> 00:12:53,540
What exactly happened?
Is a commoner really to blame?

314
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:57,580
A few days ago,
we got a summons from the chieftain.

315
00:12:58,750 --> 00:13:01,540
He wanted us to let commoners join the boar hunt.

316
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:03,130
But why?

317
00:13:03,710 --> 00:13:06,460
Boar meat is valuable to them.

318
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:09,670
Although the majority of it is given to the baron,

319
00:13:10,170 --> 00:13:12,210
the leftovers get split between us hunters.

320
00:13:12,790 --> 00:13:16,580
Of course, there are times we may trade it
for salt, firewood, or other essentials.

321
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:18,290
But it's hard to come by otherwise.

322
00:13:19,170 --> 00:13:23,040
In spite of that, no commoner
has ever volunteered themselves for a hunt.

323
00:13:23,750 --> 00:13:27,040
It's just too dangerous.
There are casualties every year.

324
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:32,000
Yet we serfs still do it, anyway.
Because it's how we make a living.

325
00:13:32,630 --> 00:13:34,330
We don't really have a choice in the matter.

326
00:13:34,790 --> 00:13:37,920
So how did the commoners end up
participating this time?

327
00:13:38,210 --> 00:13:42,040
Because they heard talk of a hero
among the serfs, I'm guessing.

328
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:43,830
Huh? You mean Krena?

329
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:45,460
No, I mean Rodin.

330
00:13:48,250 --> 00:13:51,880
You remember when Sir Zenof
called Rodin a legend in front of everybody?

331
00:13:52,710 --> 00:13:54,750
From what I've heard,

332
00:13:54,750 --> 00:13:58,000
Rodin is the man responsible for taking on
the most dangerous role in the hunts.

333
00:13:58,670 --> 00:14:01,330
In a way of speaking,
that became like an official endorsement.

334
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:05,580
Everyone assumed commoners would be safe
to join the hunt as long as Rodin was around.

335
00:14:06,330 --> 00:14:07,750
Now I get it...

336
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:12,210
Neither Rodin or I were comfortable
with amateurs tagging along on the hunt.

337
00:14:13,210 --> 00:14:16,000
But we're not in a position to refuse
orders from the chieftain.

338
00:14:19,830 --> 00:14:22,420
To make matters worse,
in the days leading up to the hunt

339
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:24,630
there were bums who wouldn't practice seriously.

340
00:14:25,380 --> 00:14:27,920
Probably felt like getting taught
by serfs was below them.

341
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:29,290
Attack in sync!

342
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:36,000
And then came today, the start of the hunt.

343
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:41,580
Here it comes!

344
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:47,960
We gave the commoners the easiest job:
holding the boar's attention.

345
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:50,210
But when the time ultimately came...

346
00:14:53,750 --> 00:14:54,580
You blockheads!

347
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:56,790
They threw our whole strategy out the window.

348
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:58,460
So we had to wing it.

349
00:14:59,000 --> 00:14:59,830
But...

350
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:04,670
Watch out!

351
00:15:10,250 --> 00:15:12,210
Fortunately, we managed to slay the boar.

352
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:15,670
I'll bring Rodin's share of meat tomorrow.

353
00:15:16,210 --> 00:15:19,420
Theresia. Allen. Stay strong for him.

354
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:25,290
I'm such a loser...
I haven't even been trying to help.

355
00:15:30,170 --> 00:15:32,170
Sorry, Mommy! I'll take over.

356
00:15:32,670 --> 00:15:35,380
I can handle it. You get some rest.

357
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:36,380
But...

358
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:39,290
The Great Boar!

359
00:15:39,460 --> 00:15:40,290
Rodin!

360
00:15:40,630 --> 00:15:41,420
Theresia?

361
00:15:42,290 --> 00:15:43,080
Daddy?

362
00:15:44,670 --> 00:15:46,170
Daddy!

363
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:51,790
Man... what have I been doing with myself?

364
00:15:52,750 --> 00:15:55,750
I've been totally preoccupied
with powering myself up.

365
00:15:56,830 --> 00:15:58,460
But what good is power without purpose?

366
00:16:02,830 --> 00:16:04,750
This isn't a game for these people.

367
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:10,040
It's a harsh world. They're doing
everything they can to survive in it.

368
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:16,040
I have a little brother to protect.
And another sibling on the way.

369
00:16:17,170 --> 00:16:20,130
Well, now! It's good to see you awake, Rodin!

370
00:16:20,420 --> 00:16:21,170
Thanks.

371
00:16:21,290 --> 00:16:22,750
But I'm still in bad shape.

372
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,750
Here. This is your share of meat.

373
00:16:25,210 --> 00:16:26,380
Thank you.

374
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:31,750
Don't worry about a thing. We're gonna make sure
your family is well taken care of over the winter.

375
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:33,460
Just focus on getting better.

376
00:16:33,790 --> 00:16:35,830
That's great. Sorry to burden you.

377
00:16:36,670 --> 00:16:37,540
Listen, Dad.

378
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:40,250
Just rest up and let me take over.

379
00:16:40,830 --> 00:16:41,750
I promise...

380
00:16:42,290 --> 00:16:44,080
I will keep our family safe!

381
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:07,330
Whoa there, Allen.

382
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:09,580
It's gonna be too heavy for you to carry.

383
00:17:09,710 --> 00:17:11,580
Thanks for your concern.

384
00:17:12,630 --> 00:17:13,380
Hup!

385
00:17:14,670 --> 00:17:15,170
Wha-?!

386
00:17:18,330 --> 00:17:19,630
Strong kid.

387
00:17:18,330 --> 00:17:19,630
I'll be damned...

388
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:22,330
It's time for me to drop the act.

389
00:17:22,670 --> 00:17:25,540
This village already has
an up-and-coming hero named Krena.

390
00:17:25,830 --> 00:17:29,250
So it's no problem even if a talentless serf
like me draws a little attention.

391
00:17:31,630 --> 00:17:36,380
I decided to pour every buff into my
physical stats, so I ditched all of the MP ones.

392
00:17:36,790 --> 00:17:38,670
Family comes first, period.

393
00:17:39,170 --> 00:17:42,080
Thank you, Allen.
That must have been hard to carry.

394
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:43,880
It was a cinch, Mom!

395
00:17:44,210 --> 00:17:46,710
I'm going to help harvest potatoes this afternoon.

396
00:17:46,710 --> 00:17:49,040
Mister Gerda said he would teach me how.

397
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:51,330
I see. Pass along my thanks to him.

398
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:56,460
Watch carefully. You pull
the potatoes up by the root.

399
00:17:56,460 --> 00:17:57,500
Wow!

400
00:17:57,500 --> 00:17:58,540
Ready to try?

401
00:17:58,710 --> 00:18:00,170
Yeah! Like this?

402
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:02,500
Not quite. You're going to need both hands to-

403
00:18:04,330 --> 00:18:06,250
Uh, never mind.

404
00:18:06,250 --> 00:18:09,580
I always knew you were a tough nut.
But you're even stronger than I thought.

405
00:18:09,830 --> 00:18:12,000
Yep. I get it from my Dad!

406
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:24,250
All that work to harvest these potatoes
and the baron gets dibs on more than half of them.

407
00:18:24,790 --> 00:18:26,670
Being a serf is rough.

408
00:18:27,290 --> 00:18:30,330
To survive the winter, we're still gonna need...

409
00:18:30,330 --> 00:18:31,790
Pardon me.

410
00:18:37,790 --> 00:18:40,460
I heard that you were back on the mend, Rodin.

411
00:18:41,170 --> 00:18:43,170
Please accept these fruits with my sympathies.

412
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:46,000
Well, thank you for your generosity.

413
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:48,080
Go on. Hurry up.

414
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,750
It's my fault! I screwed up!

415
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:52,670
Please accept my sincerest apologies!

416
00:18:52,670 --> 00:18:55,040
Ah, so this is the idiot who Dad had to save.

417
00:18:55,330 --> 00:18:57,460
Like an apology is gonna fix anything!

418
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:59,710
Be more careful next time, okay?

419
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:01,580
If you want to keep hunting, that is.

420
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:04,250
Yessir! I'll take that to heart!

421
00:19:04,670 --> 00:19:06,710
Wow, Dad's so magnanimous!

422
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:09,710
Your mistake nearly cost my husband his life.

423
00:19:10,250 --> 00:19:14,460
Everyone has a family to go back to,
no matter what their social class is.

424
00:19:15,040 --> 00:19:16,670
Please keep that in mind.

425
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:20,920
Rodin! Thank God you're okay!

426
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:24,210
He's not okay yet, dude.
But now we don't have to worry!

427
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:26,130
Let's go on another hunt, buddy!

428
00:19:26,250 --> 00:19:27,710
Dumbass! It's too soon for that!

429
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:29,080
Here, we brought a care package!

430
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:29,830
Quit pushing!

431
00:19:29,830 --> 00:19:31,960
Our wives put it together.
It should be good for you!

432
00:19:32,290 --> 00:19:35,750
Shucks, you guys.
Take it easy, he's still recovering!

433
00:19:36,210 --> 00:19:39,210
I've got the best parents in all of Japan!

434
00:19:39,330 --> 00:19:40,830
Or whatever this world is!

435
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:53,250
That should do it.

436
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,170
Summon: Hopper!

437
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:01,790
Okay, now for step two.

438
00:20:06,290 --> 00:20:07,790
Alright! Use Provoke!

439
00:20:10,170 --> 00:20:12,170
I know it's the most cliche trap ever.

440
00:20:12,330 --> 00:20:15,330
But as long as it scores me
about 50 ducks or wild birds,

441
00:20:15,330 --> 00:20:16,920
then my family can survive the winter.

442
00:20:17,330 --> 00:20:18,830
C'mon, suckers!

443
00:20:22,130 --> 00:20:24,500
Ribbit! Ribbit!

444
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:28,670
Crap. Is the range of their skill not wide enough?

445
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:32,500
This isn't working. I guess it's
back to the drawing board for me.

446
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:33,580
Huh?

447
00:20:34,330 --> 00:20:35,830
Wild bird incoming!

448
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:37,210
Bring it on!

449
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:38,630
Wait...

450
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:47,080
No... no freakin' way.

451
00:20:48,170 --> 00:20:50,040
Is that an albaheron?!

452
00:20:50,330 --> 00:20:53,790
I figured they'd just lure a few birds,
not a B-rank monster!

453
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:56,420
That's the monster I was named after.

454
00:20:56,420 --> 00:20:59,170
It looks pretty tough. I better run for it.

455
00:21:00,750 --> 00:21:02,920
HP:

456
00:21:00,750 --> 00:21:02,920
MP:

457
00:21:00,750 --> 00:21:02,920
ATTACK:

458
00:21:00,750 --> 00:21:02,920
ENDURANCE:

459
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:03,080
My enhance skill is up to level two now.

460
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:04,960
That can boost creature stats

461
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:06,290
AGILITY:

462
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:06,290
INTELLIGENCE:

463
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:06,290
LUCK:

464
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:06,290
from plus 10 to plus 20.

465
00:21:06,290 --> 00:21:09,290
And I've already enhanced
every summon in my inventory.

466
00:21:09,830 --> 00:21:11,000
It's worth a shot.

467
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:14,830
I could help provide for my family, and besides...

468
00:21:15,420 --> 00:21:17,330
hardcore gamers never shy away from a challenge!

469
00:21:23,040 --> 00:21:24,000
Summon: Fido!

470
00:21:29,790 --> 00:21:31,420
Finally, a chance to use them in real battle!

471
00:21:31,420 --> 00:21:33,210
Get wrecked, birdbrain!

472
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:39,710
Aw, hell...

473
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:41,750
Screw it!

474
00:21:44,630 --> 00:21:47,040
Man, that hit me way harder than before!

475
00:21:48,250 --> 00:21:49,290
Oh, right.

476
00:21:49,710 --> 00:21:52,630
I've been losing buffs from each
summon creature that gets defeated.

477
00:21:52,750 --> 00:21:55,170
And it's making me weaker!

478
00:21:57,380 --> 00:22:00,540
Okay, so that's one major downside
to being a Summoner...

479
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:06,460
Oh crap!

480
00:22:08,460 --> 00:22:10,170
This might be the end for me!

